    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d479">

                <pb facs="0650" n="576" xml:id="pg576"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/7608a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        British Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Spring Rice</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d479-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1877</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 6, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Ref erring to previous
                    correspondence concerning the Inter-Ally Council, I have the honor to inform you
                    that, with the approval of the President, Mr. Oscar
                        T. Crosby, Assistant Secretary of the Treasury, has been
                    designated to act as the delegate to represent the United States in the council,
                    and that, in deference to the desire of the Governments expressed by their
                    agents at this capital, the Government of the United States has no objection to
                    having its representative accept the presidency of the council when
                    organized.</p>
                <p>Mr. Crosby, who will be the sole delegate
                    of the United States, will have the assistance of a staff of advisers. He will
                    proceed to London within a few days, but I should be grateful if you would
                    kindly consider this information confidential until the announcement of Mr.
                        Crosby’s arrival in England has been
                    made.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d479-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d479-f1-content">
                <p>The same, on the same date, to the French (No. 1991), Russian (No. 26), and
                    Italian (No. 345) Ambassadors, the Belgian (No. 34) and Serbian (No. 12)
                    Ministers, and the Italian Ambassador in charge of Rumanian interests (No.
                    346).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
